# The Rust port's files stay LF in every checkout, also on Windows with
# core.autocrlf (as GitHub's Windows runners have it):
# `node rs/parity.gen.mjs --check` compares rs/parity.json and the fixtures
# byte for byte, the parity job runs rs/parity/*.sh in Git Bash, and the
# binary compiles rs/src/auth_setup.txt in, so a CR LF checkout would print
# `onenote auth setup` with CR LF where the TypeScript prints LF.
rs/** text=auto eol=lf
